======

Step 1: Find the Outlier

Example:

| Student |   Marks |
| ------- | ------: |
| A       |      78 |
| B       |      80 |
| C       |      79 |
| D       | **250** |


We identify 250 as an outlier.

Step 2: Ask "Why is it an outlier?"

Before changing the data, ask:

Is it a typing mistake?
Is it a machine/sensor error?
Is it a real event?
Is it valid business data?

=========


Step 3: Choose the Correct Action

There are several options.

Option 1: Remove the Outlier

If the value is completely wrong.

Example:

| Quantity Sold |
| ------------: |
|            52 |
|            55 |
|            58 |
|     **10000** |


f 10000 was entered by mistake, remove that row.

df = df[df["quantity_sold"] != 10000]

✅ Used when the value is clearly incorrect.

Option 2: Replace with Median (Most Common)

| Quantity Sold |
| ------------: |
|            52 |
|            55 |
|            58 |
|           300 |


Replace 300 with the median.

Before:

52
55
58
300

After:

52
55
58
56
median = df["quantity_sold"].median()

df.loc[df["quantity_sold"] > upper, "quantity_sold"] = median

✅ This is one of the most common preprocessing techniques.

=======

ption 3: Replace with Mean

Example:

mean = df["quantity_sold"].mean()

df.loc[df["quantity_sold"] > upper, "quantity_sold"] = mean

Use this when the data is approximately symmetric.


Option 4: Replace with Upper/Lower Limit (Capping)

Instead of removing the value, cap it.

Example:

Upper limit = 80

Before:

300

After:

80
df.loc[df["quantity_sold"] > upper, "quantity_sold"] = upper

This is called Winsorization.

=========

Option 5: Keep the Outlier

Sometimes the value is real.

Example:

Daily sales:

| Day       |    Sales |
| --------- | -------: |
| Monday    |      100 |
| Tuesday   |      110 |
| Wednesday | **1200** |


If Wednesday was a festival sale, then 1200 is a real business event.

Don't remove it.

Which Method is Best?

| Situation                      | Action                       |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------- |
| Typing mistake                 | Remove                       |
| Sensor error                   | Replace                      |
| Missing measurement            | Replace                      |
| Real business event            | Keep                         |
| Machine Learning preprocessing | Median replacement is common |


